Join us as an Environmental Analyst 1 and make a difference today!

The State of Connecticu t , Department of Public Health (DPH), is seeking a qualified individual for the position of Environmental Analyst 1 to work within the Environmental Laboratory Certification Program (ELCP). The ELCP is responsible for certifying laboratories that test a variety of environmental contaminants including, but not limited to, air, water, soil, sediments, and wastes. This is accomplished by a system of on-site inspections, proficiency test (PT) samples, and document review (i.e. Lab QA Plans and SOPs). Additionally, the ELCP conducts compliance investigations.

Position Highlights

Location: 410 Capitol Avenue, Hartford, CT
Work Schedule: Monday - Friday
Work Shift: Full-time, First Shift
Work Hours: 35 hours per week
A flex schedule and an opportunity to telework in accordance with State policies may be permitted following the successful completion of a working test period.

What We Can Offer You

Visit our new State Employee Benefits Overview page!
Professional growth and development opportunities
A healthy work/life balance to all employees

Duties

Under the
direct supervision of a Supervising Environmental Analyst, this position will be responsible for duties that will include, but are not limited to:

Assist with analyzing documentation associated with quarterly Environmental Laboratory renewals;
Assist with the Annual proficiency test data assessment and develop a process for data collection;
Assist with new laboratory applications and documentation;
Assist with Laboratory Director applications;
Assist with the coordination of on-site assessments;
Assist with conducting on-site assessments for non-drinking water environmental laboratories;
Assist with laboratory communications;
Assist with drafting regulation updates;
Assist and coordinate program updates;
Participate with the advisory committee;
Participate in applicable webinars; and
Perform other program related duties.

More About The Agency

The Mission of the Department of Public Health (DPH) is to protect and improve the health and safety of the people of Connecticut by:

Assuring the conditions in which people can be healthy
Preventing disease, injury, and disability
Promoting the equal enjoyment of the highest attainable standard of health, which is a human right and a priority of the state.

DPH accomplishes this through the implementation of its Strategic Plan which outlines the actions that DPH is taking to accomplish its Mission.

